      "worked_solution": "Consider the point $B.$ We can take an open interval of $x$-values such that $B$ will be the highest point on the graph in this interval. Hence, $B$ is a local maximum.\n\nA similar interval exists for the point $D,$ too. Hence, $D$ is also a local maximum.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227500/assets/260f30379f71c006b43ec6eb26200ced27a4b40aec938140d6a4cd06910ba02c.png)",
